  "leakage_audit": {
    "formula": "implied_range = battery_capacity_kWh * 1000 / efficiency_wh_per_km",
    "pearson_correlation": 0.9321,
    "median_abs_percentage_diff": 18.94,
    "mean_abs_percentage_diff": 18.77,
    "share_within_5_percent": 11.3,
    "share_within_10_percent": 20.71,
    "plain_language_conclusion": "The physical implied range (Battery Capacity \u00d7 1000 / Efficiency) exhibits a strong positive Pearson correlation of 0.9321 with listed range, with 20.7% of vehicles within 10% deviation. Because efficiency figures in automotive databases are frequently derived from standard cycle tests alongside official range ratings, keeping efficiency in the model feature set introduces substantial physical proxy information. Therefore, while efficiency is maintained in the primary feature set, a strict ablation analysis without efficiency is conducted to evaluate pure specification-based predictive capability.",
    "leakage_note": "Note: A near-deterministic physical relationship exists between battery capacity, energy consumption rate, and range. High R\u00b2 values in models including efficiency partly reflect this physical definition rather than purely independent predictive skill on latent vehicle dynamics."
  },
